  "details": "On loading VRChat the white box for VRChat.exe comes up for 2/3 mins and then is not responding and close. In the error log it mentions;\n\nUnityPlayer.dll caused a Breakpoint (0x80000003)\n  in module UnityPlayer.dll at 0033:89f976fb.\n\nand;\n\nNo mono DLL path set. This app is either running IL2CPP, or the crash occurred before mono was initialized.\n\nI have been in contact with VRChat support for over a month and 40+ emails later and trying all sorts of things to try to fix it even fresh windows install. Support team have given in and ask me to file a bug report.\n\nIf anyone can help please do.",
